.,12\\}$ using a conditional definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,{{field-2}}\\le x\\le {{field-3}}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-6$ and $12$ (including $-6$ and $12$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,-6\\le x\\le 12\\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $-7<x<13.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS=\\{x\\in Z\\,:\\,-7<x<13\\}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d75edb12-98ba-52db-b23a-45b102a7c2b9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418463}}] :activity/title "Describing Sets Using Set-Builder Notation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418460}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435005} :activity/id #uuid "55d163d3-8f28-5869-a65b-cfaaab7569eb" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049076 :topic/id #uuid "d8ad0390-dfee-58d8-ac50-00cbfdc660af" :topic/math-academy-id 4393} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435004 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8858ad30-a1fc-5136-97b2-1c0e818522eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196497} {:answer/id #uuid "0ffd3501-b258-5c11-bccd-bfa4138ce20a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "Z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196498} {:answer/id #uuid "68b3b0b4-5207-504a-9560-62f599a49306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196499}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186196499} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b9bed19-3128-508d-b4d4-f5e8ece817d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1992cc29-bfe9-5821-ab65-85db7c9275d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435000} {:answer/id #uuid "288cc4b2-c914-5214-82ea-49b388ebac4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435001} {:answer/id #uuid "cde8a085-4109-5cb9-b7e6-882a1aca743e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5\\cdot {2}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435002} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe45b33-5883-51ed-9f7c-2fa52c2e29d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {5}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435003}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435000} :answer-field/id #uuid "66c4793e-1f9c-549e-b450-2f3a6b0a8958" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186196500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d9cd56d9-afeb-5bee-b832-904b834a28b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-183783" :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\{-5,-10,-20,-40,...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n$$\nS=\\{{{field-1}}\\,:\\,n\\in {{field-2}}\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n-5,\\,-10,\\,-20,\\,-40,\\,…\n$$\n\nform an infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =2 \\\\  & =\\frac{-10}{-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20}{-10} \\\\  & =\\frac{-40}{-20} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in N,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot {2}^{n}\\cdot {2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS=\\{-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {2}^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in N\\}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3a19ba88-b779-5826-958c-8abfa367305b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435007}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435005 :step/content {:db/